tems segments. The company offers engineering services to telecommunications providers, including the planning and design of aerial, underground, and buried fiber optic, copper, and coaxial cable systems; placement of cables, related structures, and drop lines for telephone companies and cable multiple system operators; program and project management, and inspection personnel; and wireless networks in connection with the deployment of macro cell and new small cell sites. It also provides construction, maintenance, and installation services, such as placement and splicing of copper, fiber, and coaxial cables; tower construction, lines and antenna installation, foundation and equipment pad construction, and small cell site placement for wireless carriers, as well as equipment installation and material fabrication, and site testing services; underground facility locating services, including locating telephone, cable television, power, water, sewer, and gas lines for utility companies; installation and maintenance of customer premise equipment for electric and gas utilities, and other customers. Dycom Industries, Inc. was incorporated in 1969 and is based in West Palm Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel S. Peyovich | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $284K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Dycom Industries, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.2B market cap on $5.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and 